{"campaign_id": "81a5458d-ce8f-4c03-b9d2-8ce4f1ff9e9e", "completed_at": "2026-10-09T12:05:37Z", "error": null, "id": "M1", "inquiry_id": null, "kind": "measurement", "request": {"description": "Measure the compiled MuJoCo arm dynamics, actuator authority, reversal and braking response, and joint-limit reactions without requiring a learned candidate.", "measurements": [{"args": ["--artifact", "campaigns/evaluations/81a5458d-ce8f-4c03-b9d2-8ce4f1ff9e9e/compiled_dynamics.json"], "artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/81a5458d-ce8f-4c03-b9d2-8ce4f1ff9e9e/compiled_dynamics.json", "instrument": "python_module", "label": "initial compiled dynamics and limit characterization", "module": "robot_learning.lab.compiled_dynamics"}], "rationale": "The initial decision is whether the likely route to 98% success should first address mechanical reach-and-hold constraints or proceed with policy learning. The physical model leaves effective inertia, actuator realization, and native limit behavior unresolved; these measurements directly discriminate whether poor hold performance would be plausibly caused by weak authority, slow reversals, or limit reactions. High authority and benign limits support a baseline learning route followed by hold diagnostics; low authority, long braking, or active limits redirect the route toward control-aware training and branch selection."}, "result": {"measurements": [{"args": ["--artifact", "campaigns/evaluations/81a5458d-ce8f-4c03-b9d2-8ce4f1ff9e9e/compiled_dynamics.json"], "instrument": "python_module", "label": "initial compiled dynamics and limit characterization", "metrics": {"evaluation_artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/81a5458d-ce8f-4c03-b9d2-8ce4f1ff9e9e/python-module-M1-1-compiled_dynamics.json", "evaluation_artifact_contents": {"scope": "structure_only", "sections": [{"entries": 7, "path": "", "type": "object"}, {"path": "/schema_version", "type": "number"}, {"path": "/measurement", "type": "string"}, {"path": "/model_source", "type": "string"}, {"